  "gameData": {
    "backstory": "Hatchling, as he's known, isn't old enough to remember the Old World, only the smoldering decay of Subchain City. Found as an egg near the Burnt Bean refinery, he unfortunately hatched with a mysterious, plague-like affliction - strangely, it seems to empower him, making him both feared and pitied.",
    "class": "Plaguebringer",
    "name": "Hatchling Plague",
    "personality": "Grimly Determined: Hatchling witnessed brutality at a young age. He is quiet, intense, and focused solely on the survival, and maybe someday thriving, of his flock. Resourceful: Scavenging is his forte. He's mastered the art of finding usable scraps amidst the ruins, often turning trash into surprisingly effective gear. Vengeful: Consumed by the need to protect his allies, he is a nightmare to enemies or anyone causing harm to his flock.",
    "specialAbility": {
      "description": "Hatchling emits a toxic cloud that weakens enemy defenses and makes them open to critical hits. This affliction can also spread across adjacent enemies if they have a low resistance to the plague.",
